+ * wake it. Without that, nearly every release took the wait lock, in the
+ * mutex's own cache line, to wake a task that was running anyway
+ * (locktorture mutex_lock, 128 writers on 64 CPUs: 720 000 wake_up_q()
+ * calls per second, 4 300 schedule() calls). The flag is cleared with a
+ * full barrier before the caller looks at the lock again and before it
